From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shupeng Xue <dspxue@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 04:13:38 +1100
Subject: [PATCH wireless-next 12/12] wifi: b43: raise BCM4331 HT PCIe read
 requests to 512 bytes

With MRRS 128, large BCM4331 HT A-MPDUs repeatedly underflow the TX
FIFO even next to the AP. The same hardware running wl uses MRRS 512;
loading b43 afterwards retains that setting and avoids the regression.

On an uncapped aggregate test, changing only the endpoint Device
Control MRRS field from 128 to 512 restores TCP TX from 72-87 to
169-171 Mbps and removes 590-642 underflows per 12 seconds. Changing
it back reproduces the slow throughput and underflows. RX is mostly
unchanged. This isolates the PCIe request size rather than RSSI, AP
configuration or a different driver binary.

For BCM4331 HT TX aggregation on a BCMA PCIe host, request MRRS 512
after host PCI setup and before DMA initialization. Use the PCI API
to honor host-bridge restrictions and the performance-mode MPS clamp.
Do not lower an already larger MRRS, modify other endpoints or alter
the unrelated BCMA PCI-core hostmode limit. Keep adaptive aggregate
limiting as fallback if the request fails or remains platform-clamped.
PIO, non-PCI hosts and legacy HT modes retain their existing behavior.
Controller restart and resume reinitialization revisit the setting.

Tested on BCM4331/Linux 6.18.54 HT40 with adaptive limiting retained:
TCP TX 169-170, UDP TX 215-216 Mbps, no observed FIFO underflows;
reconnect and controller restart retain MRRS 512. A 600-second TCP TX
run averages 168 Mbps with zero underflows and zero MAC txphyerr.
System suspend/resume and other platforms are not hardware-tested.

Fixes: 19f136286203 ("b43: HT-PHY: 5 GHz, 802.11n and the rest (not yet split, not for submission)")
Assisted-by: pi:gpt-6.1-sol
---
 drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/b43/main.c | 32 ++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 32 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/b43/main.c b/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/b43/main.c
index 49bdd8bfa72e..9f75ed75ec3b 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/b43/main.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/b43/main.c
@@ -5192,6 +5192,35 @@ static void b43_wireless_core_exit(struct b43_wldev *dev)
 	b43_bus_may_powerdown(dev);
 }
 
+#if defined(CONFIG_B43_BCMA) && defined(CONFIG_BCMA_HOST_PCI)
+static void b43_bcma_set_readrq(struct b43_wldev *dev)
+{
+	struct bcma_bus *bus = dev->dev->bdev->bus;
+	struct pci_dev *pdev;
+	int err;
+
+	if (dev->dev->chip_id != BCMA_CHIP_ID_BCM4331 ||
+	    dev->phy.type != B43_PHYTYPE_HT ||
+	    bus->hosttype != BCMA_HOSTTYPE_PCI || modparam_htphy_11n < 2 ||
+	    dev->use_pio)
+		return;
+	pdev = bus->host_pci;
+	if (!pci_is_pcie(pdev) || pcie_get_readrq(pdev) >= 512)
+		return;
+
+	/* At MRRS 128, large HT A-MPDUs repeatedly underflow the TX FIFO.
+	 * A 512-byte request size eliminates this on the tested BCM4331, matching
+	 * the PCIe state left by wl. Use the PCI API so bridge restrictions
+	 * remain authoritative; adaptive limiting handles a smaller MRRS.
+	 */
+	err = pcie_set_readrq(pdev, 512);
+	if (err)
+		b43warn(dev->wl, "Cannot raise PCIe MRRS to 512 bytes (%d)\n", err);
+	else if (pcie_get_readrq(pdev) < 512)
+		b43warn(dev->wl, "PCIe MRRS remains below 512 bytes\n");
+}
+#endif
+
 /* Initialize a wireless core */
 static int b43_wireless_core_init(struct b43_wldev *dev)
 {
@@ -5219,6 +5248,9 @@ static int b43_wireless_core_init(struct b43_wldev *dev)
 		bcma_host_pci_irq_ctl(dev->dev->bdev->bus,
 				      dev->dev->bdev, true);
 		bcma_host_pci_up(dev->dev->bdev->bus);
+#ifdef CONFIG_BCMA_HOST_PCI
+		b43_bcma_set_readrq(dev);
+#endif
 		break;
 #endif
 #ifdef CONFIG_B43_SSB
